-- Playbook ve-pricing-points-passport: Earn your Passport build record, part 4 (Logan, 2026-11-01). Safe to run twice.
insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-pricing-points-passport', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-01 (Logan). Earn your Passport, part 4 built and live: the three challenges (Sean: "continue Earn your Passport").
4. THE CHALLENGES. /challenges: Support Local, The Connector and The Advocate, Start, 30 days, one restart, 1,100 points each. Start makes the sign-in account for a Taster whose email is confirmed (a members row waiting on its Passport, no password; its session kept apart from the site's sign-in, so the site still treats them as signed out); once a member they set a password on the page or use Google. Support Local: 3 food places with How Vegan set, each with a check-in menu item approved in Depot > Check-ins, and one approved receipt; in a stops month only the chapter's stops count; challengers' check-ins pay 0 points. The Connector: 3 friends who pay to join through their link during the 30 days. The Advocate: a free event (a photo, or a guest pass checked in), a sanctuary or rescue (a photo, the phone's distance kept), a share of a Fosters or Rescues post or a rescue's page (the boards had no posts yet). Settling on every read, each approval and every 15 minutes: the first one finished spends its 1,100 on the Passport (lifetime keeps them) and makes them a member (Founding before the deadline); each after adds 1,100; all three is Trailblazer. Depot > Challenges reviews The Advocate's proofs and shows every challenge. Migration 20261101_earn_your_passport_challenges.sql (through ve-once-challenges, now the 410 stub); ve-challenge and ve-checkin from commit 9825760 (sha256 matched). Proven live with [TEST] Tasters, desktop and phone; every test row and photo removed.
LOGAN'S DEFAULTS, SEAN'S TO CHANGE: who may take them (not a paying member; an earned member may finish the others), food places only for Support Local, a restart keeps approved work, a rescue's page counts as a share, no check-in points while a challenger.
NEXT: 5. the two-day business follow-up and the not-ready-yet emails, 6. the content gig, 7. the business points rule.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-pricing-points-passport' and body like 'BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-01 (Logan). Earn your Passport, part 4%');
